# Extra redaction patterns for redact_jsonc.py -- copy to
# redact-extra-patterns.txt, which .gitignore excludes from this public repo.
#
# One Python regex per line, matched case-insensitively against every string in
# the settings file, as a value and as a key. A matching value is replaced with
# the placeholder; a matching key is dropped along with its value.
#
# This is where internal project, service and host names go. They cannot live
# in redact_jsonc.py's own VALUE_PATTERNS, because that file is committed --
# naming them there would publish the very identifiers the rule exists to hide.
#
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored. Bad regexes are reported and skipped.

# Internal project names that show up in interpreter and virtualenv paths:
# my-internal-project
# some-service-name

# An internal domain that extensions record as an endpoint:
# \.corp\.example\.com\b
